Chapter: BundledAgentTest
  cites Works chapter AgentBundle

 Boots with a GPT image attached whose FAT16 ESP holds AGENT.GGU and a signed
 AGENT.MAN, and prints the verdict of the whole bundled-agent chain.

 The disk is built by `build/agent-bundle-test.ps1`, which runs this same
 binary four times: once against an honest bundle and three times against
 bundles with one link of the chain broken. A single expected file cannot hold
 four answers, so this test's `.expected` pins only the honest one and the
 harness owns the negative controls. Without them a verifier that answered
 BUNDLE OK unconditionally would pass here, which is the whole failure this
 chain exists to prevent.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    v <- bundled-agent-verdict
    print-line-uni (format-bundle-verdict v)
  end
